lt;a href="#kubernetesmasterclassforapplicationdevelopers"&gt;Kubernetes Masterclass for Application Developers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#helmmasterclass_frombeginnertoadvanced"&gt;Helm Masterclass - From Beginner to Advanced&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#automationwithansible_hands-ondevops"&gt;Automation with Ansible - Hands-on DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#pythonfordevops_theultimatehands-onguide"&gt;Python for DevOps: The Ultimate Hands-On Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#practicaldevopsbootcampforall"&gt;Practical DevOps Bootcamp for All&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#gitopsinpracticewithargocdandargorollouts_thecompleteguide"&gt;GitOps in Practice with Argo CD and Argo Rollouts - The Complete Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#bt18"&gt;Pay $18 or more to also unlock!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#automateyourdevopspipelineswithgithubactions"&gt;Automate your DevOps pipelines with GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#kubernetesandcloudnativeassociatekcnawithpracticeexams"&gt;Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) with Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#cloudnativebuildpacksfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-on"&gt;Cloud Native Buildpacks for the Absolute Beginners - Hands-on&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#masteringdockeressentials_hands-ondevops"&gt;Mastering Docker Essentials - Hands-on DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#ciandcdfortestautomation_jenkinsandgithubactions"&gt;CI/CD for Test Automation: Jenkins &amp; GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#jenkinsforbeginners"&gt;Jenkins for Beginners&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#k8sgptessentials_unlockingkubernetesinsightswithai"&gt;K8sGPT Essentials - Unlocking Kubernetes Insights with AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dockerforaiandml"&gt;Docker for AI/ML&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#fluxcdfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-ondevops"&gt;Flux CD for the Absolute Beginners - Hands-On DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#terraforminaction_buildandmanagecloudinfrastructure"&gt;Terraform in Action - Build &amp; Manage Cloud Infrastructure&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dockerfordevelopers2026_microservicesprojectworkshop"&gt;Docker for Developers 2026 - Microservices Project Workshop&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#hands-onciandcdwithgithubactions_absolutepractical"&gt;Hands-On CI/CD with GitHub Actions - Absolute Practical&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#introductiontodevopsfundamentalsforitandsoftwareprofessionals"&gt;Introduction to DevOps Fundamentals for IT and Software Professionals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#designandimplementciandcdpipelinesusingjenkins_hands-on"&gt;Design &amp; Implement CI/CD Pipelines using Jenkins - Hands-On&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#devopsandgenaiusingnetazureopenaiandgithub"&gt;DevOps and GenAI using .NET, Azure OpenAI and GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#opentelemetryinpractice_thecompleteobservabilitycourse"&gt;OpenTelemetry in Practice: The Complete Observability Course&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h2 id="0"&gt;Pay $5 to unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="dockerandkubernetesmasterclass_frombeginnertoadvanced"&gt;&lt;a id="dockerandkubernetesmasterclass_frombeginnertoadvanced" href="https://youtu.be/U63VSZ2EULI"&gt;Docker and Kubernetes Masterclass: From Beginner to Advanced&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course takes you from the fundamentals of containerization to deploying and managing applications in production-ready cloud-native environments. You begin by learning Docker architecture, containers, images, Dockerfiles, registries, networking, storage, resource management, and Docker Compose. Through hands-on exercises and projects, you will containerize web applications, optimize images, manage data persistence, and build multi-container solutions using real-world workflows. The journey then progresses into Kubernetes, covering cluster architecture, pods, services, manifests, ReplicaSets, Deployments, namespaces, resource management, probes, persistent storage, StatefulSets, ConfigMaps, Secrets, RBAC, network policies, pod security standards, and Kustomize. Practical labs and projects reinforce how to deploy, scale, secure, and operate applications effectively. The course concludes with deploying applications to Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE), working with ingress, load balancing, and cloud infrastructure. New hands-on labs cover AI-assisted Dockerfile optimization, Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA), and queue-based autoscaling with custom metrics. By the end of this course, you will confidently build, optimize, deploy, secure, scale, and manage production-ready applications using Docker and Kubernetes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="cloud-native_microserviceskubernetesservicemeshciandcd"&gt;&lt;a id="cloud-native_microserviceskubernetesservicemeshciandcd" href="https://youtu.be/9rkuQ7CVIZ4"&gt;Cloud-Native - Microservices, Kubernetes, Service Mesh, CI/CD&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course provides a complete journey into cloud-native development, teaching you to design, build, and deploy modern distributed systems. Start by understanding cloud-native principles, microservices, Kubernetes, and service meshes. Through hands-on projects, learn to build RESTful APIs using AWS Lambda, API Gateway, and DynamoDB. Explore caching with Redis and ElastiCache, asynchronous communication with Kafka and RabbitMQ, and event-driven architectures for scalable solutions. Advance into Kubernetes orchestration, using horizontal scaling with HPA and event-driven scaling with KEDA. Deploy and manage workloads with Helm charts, automate infrastructure provisioning with Terraform, and create CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions. Discover observability practices with Prometheus, Grafana, and distributed tracing tools like Zipkin to monitor and troubleshoot systems effectively. With practical labs and real-world projects, this course equips you to modernize legacy systems or build cloud-native applications from scratch. Master the skills to design scalable, secure, and resilient architectures for today’s dynamic IT landscape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="practicalkubernetes_beyondckaandckadhands-on"&gt;&lt;a id="practicalkubernetes_beyondckaandckadhands-on" href="https://youtu.be/mPkNStMu9TM"&gt;Practical Kubernetes - Beyond CKA and CKAD Hands-on&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This advanced Kubernetes course is designed for professionals seeking to go beyond certification exams like CKA and CKAD. It starts by laying a solid foundation with Kubernetes architecture and cluster setup. You'll then explore essential Kubernetes objects such as Pods, ReplicaSets, and Deployments, followed by practical hands-on demonstrations for configuring and managing them effectively. As you move deeper into the course, you'll master advanced Kubernetes concepts such as scaling, networking, and application rollouts. You'll learn about persistent storage, managing StatefulSets, and cluster upgrades. Notably, new sections introduce Pod Disruption Budgets (PDBs) and Kubernetes Events, providing critical tools for maintaining availability and troubleshooting in production environments. The course culminates with advanced monitoring techniques using Prometheus and Grafana, enabling you to track and visualize Kubernetes performance metrics. You'll also learn how to automate deployments using Helm charts, secure your environment using RBAC, and implement network policies. By the end, you'll be equipped to confidently manage Kubernetes clusters in real-world scenarios, solving complex problems with best practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="terraformmastery_completehands-onguidewithinterview-readyprep"&gt;&lt;a id="terraformmastery_completehands-onguidewithinterview-readyprep" href="https://youtu.be/on4YUiZxBLQ"&gt;Terraform Mastery: Complete Hands-On Guide with Interview-Ready Prep&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course explores infrastructure automation for modern cloud environments, helping you design, manage, and scale systems using Infrastructure as Code principles. You will begin with core concepts such as IaC, Terraform architecture, and AWS integration, enabling a smooth shift from manual provisioning to efficient, automated workflows. You will then dive into Terraform fundamentals, including providers, resources, state management, variables, and dependencies. Through hands-on labs, you will build AWS infrastructure such as EC2, S3, networking, and security setups while learning modules, provisioning, and reusable design patterns. This course is ideal for aspiring DevOps engineers, cloud professionals, and developers seeking practical automation skills. A basic understanding of cloud computing and AWS will help you maximize learning and apply concepts effectively in real scenarios. By the end of this course, you will learn how to automate infrastructure, manage state securely, build scalable Terraform modules, and apply best practices to real-world cloud environments with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt12"&gt;Pay $12 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="kubernetesmasterclassforapplicationdevelopers"&gt;&lt;a id="kubernetesmasterclassforapplicationdevelopers" href="https://youtu.be/gq4E2Dhk42M"&gt;Kubernetes Masterclass for Application Developers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dive into the world of Kubernetes with our expertly crafted masterclass designed specifically for application developers. We begin with an introduction to containers, where you'll learn what makes containers special, how to install Docker, and explore creating and managing Docker images. With hands-on exercises, you'll connect multiple containers and manage them using Docker Compose. Delve into core Kubernetes concepts, exploring its architecture and the role of each component within the control plane. Practical examples will guide you through understanding Pods, their lifecycle, namespaces, and manifest files. Step-by-step instructions will help you set up a local Kubernetes cluster with Minikube, execute basic kubectl commands, and deploy your first Pod. Advance to managing Pod lifecycles, services, and Ingress. Deploy a REST API, explore Init containers, and understand probes and hooks. Learn to manage access to Pods, implement ReplicaSets and Deployments, and configure rollout strategies. Finally, discover batch workflows, configuration and secret management, and storage handling. The course concludes with deploying your app on AWS Elastic Kubernetes Service, covering cluster creation, app deployment, and access through load balancers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="helmmasterclass_frombeginnertoadvanced"&gt;&lt;a id="helmmasterclass_frombeginnertoadvanced" href="https://youtu.be/hnxfq_WNUYw"&gt;Helm Masterclass - From Beginner to Advanced&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dive into the world of Kubernetes package management with this in-depth Helm masterclass. Begin your journey by understanding the role of Helm in Kubernetes, its architecture, and how it compares to other tools. With step-by-step guidance, you’ll set up essential tools like Minikube, kubectl, and Visual Studio Code to ensure a smooth learning experience.  As you advance, you’ll master Helm’s core features, from discovering and installing charts to customizing deployments and managing releases. Learn to create custom Helm charts, leveraging Go templates and advanced templating techniques to build scalable, reusable solutions. Explore the power of Helm’s chart dependencies, subcharts, and hooks to elevate your Kubernetes projects.  By the end of the course, you’ll have the skills to confidently use Helm for managing Kubernetes resources. With a mix of theory and hands-on exercises, this course equips you to optimize deployments, troubleshoot issues, and integrate advanced features into your workflow, whether you’re a developer or DevOps professional.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="automationwithansible_hands-ondevops"&gt;&lt;a id="automationwithansible_hands-ondevops" href="https://youtu.be/4kmuMl13-zE"&gt;Automation with Ansible - Hands-on DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course immerses you in the world of automation through Ansible, a leading tool in the DevOps field. Starting with a solid foundation, you will learn the installation process, configuration, and basic functionalities of Ansible before diving into more advanced topics. The course guides you through the essentials of Ansible, such as modules, inventory, and playbooks, with hands-on demonstrations and real-world scenarios. Throughout the course, you will progress from understanding Ansible’s foundational concepts to implementing complex automation solutions. You’ll master the creation and management of Ansible playbooks, learn how to manage Windows environments, and even get familiar with advanced features like Ansible Vault and AWX for streamlined automation. Each section builds on the last, allowing you to understand both the theoretical concepts and practical applications of Ansible automation. Whether you're looking to automate your infrastructure or streamline your DevOps pipelines, this course ensures you’ll leave with the skills necessary to deploy, manage, and troubleshoot your systems effectively. By the end, you'll be equipped to leverage Ansible’s full potential and contribute meaningfully to any automation-driven project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="pythonfordevops_theultimatehands-onguide"&gt;&lt;a id="pythonfordevops_theultimatehands-onguide" href="https://youtu.be/Cm8pwyTQNyo"&gt;Python for DevOps: The Ultimate Hands-On Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course starts by guiding learners through setting up a Python environment tailored for DevOps tasks, covering version management, virtual environments, and interactive coding with JupyterLab. Students build a strong foundation in Python, including variables, loops, functions, data structures, and object-oriented programming, with practical DevOps exercises like disk usage calculation and log management. As the course progresses, learners dive into advanced Python features for DevOps, such as generators, decorators, exception handling, resource management, and logging practices. They gain hands-on experience with APIs, file handling, parsing JSON/YAML/CSV data, automating operations, and securely managing environment variables. The final sections focus on professional-grade development practices, including static typing, automated testing with Pytest, project structuring, and CI/CD pipeline creation. Students design command-line interfaces, integrate GitHub Actions workflows, implement linting and security checks, and automate deployment to PyPI. By the end, learners will be ready to solve complex DevOps challenges using Python, creating scalable, efficient, and automated solutions for modern infrastructures.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="practicaldevopsbootcampforall"&gt;&lt;a id="practicaldevopsbootcampforall" href="https://youtu.be/llpKnMCet6k"&gt;Practical DevOps Bootcamp for All&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Embark on an exciting journey through the DevOps lifecycle, where you’ll gain practical, real-world skills in GitHub, Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, and CI/CD automation. The course starts with planning and version control using Git, followed by setting up a cloud infrastructure on AWS. You’ll dive deep into containerization with Docker and learn how to orchestrate and scale applications using Kubernetes. The curriculum is designed to provide step-by-step guidance, including hands-on demonstrations for setting up environments, deploying Python Flask applications, and scaling them for production. Throughout the course, you’ll explore real-time troubleshooting, providing you with the ability to handle DevOps challenges effectively. By the end of this course, you’ll be confident in using industry-standard DevOps tools. You’ll gain experience with GitHub Actions for automation, Prometheus for monitoring, and Grafana for visualization. This journey will empower you to apply DevOps principles in real-world scenarios and contribute to efficient application development and deployment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="gitopsinpracticewithargocdandargorollouts_thecompleteguide"&gt;&lt;a id="gitopsinpracticewithargocdandargorollouts_thecompleteguide" href="https://youtu.be/-s1buNOKiWE"&gt;GitOps in Practice with Argo CD and Argo Rollouts - The Complete Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course is designed for professionals aiming to enhance their skills in modern application deployment and management with GitOps. It covers Argo CD, a powerful continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes, and Argo Rollouts, which enhances application deployment strategies. Learners will gain a solid understanding of core GitOps principles, Argo CD’s architecture, and best practices for scaling deployments. In the first part, you will learn the fundamentals of GitOps, the drawbacks of traditional deployment models, and how Argo CD helps streamline these processes. Through labs and real-world examples, you will install and configure Argo CD, exploring key features like application CRD, syncing, and health status management. Following this, the course delves into advanced features such as Helm integration, sync automation, and managing private repositories. By the end of the course, you will be proficient in orchestrating complex deployments with Argo CD and Argo Rollouts, leveraging strategies like Blue-Green and Canary for traffic management. This course provides a complete roadmap for DevOps engineers to implement GitOps successfully in their infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt18"&gt;Pay $18 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="automateyourdevopspipelineswithgithubactions"&gt;&lt;a id="automateyourdevopspipelineswithgithubactions" href="https://youtu.be/kgFG3QWfMus"&gt;Automate your DevOps pipelines with GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course begins with the fundamentals of GitHub Actions, guiding you through the creation of your first workflow and how to include inputs. You’ll quickly advance to developing workflows specifically for .NET applications, building pipelines that can deploy to Azure. As you progress, you will gain practical experience in deploying infrastructure using Terraform and Bicep, learning to deploy and manage cloud resources directly from GitHub Actions. As you move deeper into the course, you’ll explore containerization and deployment, including pushing Docker images to container registries and integrating these steps into GitHub Actions workflows. You'll also dive into Kubernetes/AKS, learning the essentials of CI/CD pipelines for containerized applications, and building, pushing, and deploying images to Kubernetes clusters. The course also introduces cutting-edge GitHub Actions features like self-hosted runners, reusable workflows, and passwordless workflows using OIDC. It further expands your knowledge with advanced security features, such as GitHub Advanced Security and integrating Microsoft Defender for DevOps. By the end of the course, you will have the expertise to build robust and secure DevOps pipelines that automate the full software delivery lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="kubernetesandcloudnativeassociatekcnawithpracticeexams"&gt;&lt;a id="kubernetesandcloudnativeassociatekcnawithpracticeexams" href="https://youtu.be/yJtscjWtTgs"&gt;Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) with Practice Exams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course is designed to guide you through the Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam preparation. It starts with an introduction to containers, cloud-native computing, and Kubernetes evolution. You’ll explore Kubernetes components like Pods, Deployments, ReplicaSets, and Services, building a solid foundation in container orchestration. Practical demonstrations and labs help you apply concepts to real-world scenarios.  As you progress, you'll dive into Kubernetes networking, object definitions, and best practices. Key topics such as Kubernetes security, storage, scheduling, and application delivery are thoroughly covered. The course also introduces Helm, Service Meshes, and observability tools like Prometheus and Grafana, preparing you for cloud-native infrastructure management.  Hands-on demonstrations and optional labs provide opportunities to practice setting up clusters, configuring services, and managing resources. The course wraps up with practice exams to test your knowledge and ensure you’re ready for the KCNA certification.  Anyone who wants to get familiar with the Containerization basics and Docker Fundamentals may refer this section - “Understanding Docker (Optional)” or if you are already familiar with Docker then feel free to skip this section.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="cloudnativebuildpacksfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-on"&gt;&lt;a id="cloudnativebuildpacksfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-on" href="https://youtu.be/mSItJSR_14k"&gt;Cloud Native Buildpacks for the Absolute Beginners - Hands-on&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course begins by establishing a strong foundation in container images and the role of Buildpacks in modern application deployment. Early modules provide clarity on what Buildpacks are, their key features, and essential terminology, ensuring learners build a solid conceptual understanding. With clear demonstrations, users will navigate official documentation and essential tools like the Pack CLI, tailored for multiple operating systems. Progressing through practical applications, the course dives into building container images for popular languages including Python, Node.js, and Java. These demonstrations highlight how Buildpacks streamline complex workflows like integrating databases and managing build lifecycles. The hands-on approach ensures learners not only understand theoretical concepts but also gain real-world skills. Advanced sections focus on empowering users to create their own Buildpacks and Builders, with step-by-step guidance on customization and Procfile usage. The course culminates with an exploration of kpack, a Kubernetes-native Buildpack tool, showcasing environment setup, cluster configuration, and image publishing workflows. Throughout, learners are supported with detailed walkthroughs, preparing them to deploy cloud-native applications efficiently and confidently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="masteringdockeressentials_hands-ondevops"&gt;&lt;a id="masteringdockeressentials_hands-ondevops" href="https://youtu.be/XUGb0Ky55YE"&gt;Mastering Docker Essentials - Hands-on DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mastering Docker Essentials is designed for developers eager to dive into the world of containerization and DevOps with Docker. This course begins with a solid foundation, covering core Docker concepts like containers, images, and volumes, providing you with the knowledge to begin deploying applications seamlessly across environments. The hands-on exercises guide you through real-world examples, ensuring you grasp the practical applications of Docker from day one. As you progress, you'll explore more advanced topics such as Docker networking and volumes, which are essential for managing multi-container environments. The course also delves into optimizing Docker images through Dockerfiles, while demonstrating how to integrate Docker Compose for managing multi-container applications. Each section is geared toward ensuring you can build, manage, and scale Docker containers effectively and efficiently in your development lifecycle. Throughout the course, you'll leverage various environments, including local setups, Docker Hub, and even cloud-based Docker deployments, providing you with a holistic learning experience. By the end of this course, you'll be confident in deploying applications with Docker, managing containerized environments, and utilizing Docker's most powerful features in production.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="ciandcdfortestautomation_jenkinsandgithubactions"&gt;&lt;a id="ciandcdfortestautomation_jenkinsandgithubactions" href="https://youtu.be/G4uF7A7Noho"&gt;CI/CD for Test Automation: Jenkins &amp; GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this course, you'll learn how to leverage Jenkins and GitHub Actions to automate tests and streamline CI/CD pipelines. Starting with CI/CD fundamentals, you’ll explore key concepts and tools before diving into hands-on setup for both Jenkins and GitHub Actions. You’ll build test automation pipelines that include unit tests, API, E2E, and performance testing, ensuring continuous testing throughout the development lifecycle. The course covers setting up complex test strategies, publishing test results, and managing thresholds for optimal test automation. You’ll also learn to deploy the BugTracker app manually, via Jenkins, and GitHub Actions to simulate real-world deployment workflows. Perfect for developers, QA engineers, and testers, this course offers practical examples and deep insights into CI/CD best practices, helping you enhance testing workflows, automation, and collaboration. Whether enhancing your skills or implementing automation in your team, this course provides everything you need to master CI/CD practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="jenkinsforbeginners"&gt;&lt;a id="jenkinsforbeginners" href="https://youtu.be/pFTXore2gCE"&gt;Jenkins for Beginners&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this beginner-friendly course, you'll learn how to harness the power of Jenkins to automate your software development processes. Starting with the basics, you'll explore Jenkins' role in Continuous Integration and Continuous Delivery (CI/CD), and gain an understanding of its architecture and key features. The course will guide you through setting up Jenkins, from installation to navigating the user interface, and show you how to create and run projects using Freestyle Jobs. You’ll also learn how to link multiple jobs together to streamline workflows. As the course progresses, you'll dive into Jenkins pipelines, where you’ll discover how to define them using Jenkinsfiles, configure advanced pipeline settings, and integrate with Source Code Management (SCM) tools like Git. You’ll also explore Blue Ocean for visual pipeline creation and learn to manage pipeline parameters for dynamic execution. The course also covers automation using Jenkins CLI and APIs, allowing you to automate tasks programmatically. Security is emphasized, with practical lessons on CSRF protection, role-based access control, and secure Jenkins configuration. By the end, you'll have the knowledge and skills to implement Jenkins for automating, testing, and securing your software development pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="k8sgptessentials_unlockingkubernetesinsightswithai"&gt;&lt;a id="k8sgptessentials_unlockingkubernetesinsightswithai" href="https://youtu.be/IbMexf0Pc-o"&gt;K8sGPT Essentials - Unlocking Kubernetes Insights with AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course helps professionals integrate Kubernetes (K8s) with AI through K8sGPT, an advanced tool offering AI-powered analysis of K8s clusters. You will begin by exploring K8sGPT's features, learning how it enhances Kubernetes management with improved documentation, real-time issue detection, and problem-solving automation. Practical demonstrations will guide you through installing and configuring K8sGPT on macOS and Kubernetes clusters. As you progress, you’ll learn how to effectively set up K8sGPT in different environments, use its command-line interface (CLI), and execute commands like analyze and filter. You’ll also explore integrating K8sGPT with leading AI platforms like Google Gemini and Amazon Bedrock. The course covers K8sGPT's core terminologies, processes, and its interaction with popular tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and KubeBuddy. The course includes hands-on demonstrations that showcase how to troubleshoot and enhance K8s dashboards with AI-driven insights. You’ll gain practical experience with in-cluster operator workflows, learning to scale, monitor, and automate Kubernetes clusters. By the end of the course, you’ll be equipped to optimize Kubernetes environments and leverage K8sGPT for powerful automation and analysis in your workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="dockerforaiandml"&gt;&lt;a id="dockerforaiandml" href="https://youtu.be/YpNSYOpqANQ"&gt;Docker for AI/ML&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this course, you’ll master Docker for AI/ML development, deployment, and maintenance. The course begins with an introduction to Docker’s significance in machine learning and AI, demonstrating how containers provide reproducibility and scalability. You will set up Docker environments to run ML tools, including Jupyter, MLFlow, and more, preparing you for tasks like packaging models and deploying them on production systems. The curriculum is structured around practical, project-based learning. You will progress from setting up basic ML environments to packaging ML applications as containerized images. The course dives into Dockerfiles, container operations, and how to integrate services using Docker Compose, allowing you to simulate production-grade systems. By exploring projects, such as deploying a house price prediction app or running LLMs locally, you’ll manage complex workflows in Docker. You’ll also explore Docker’s Model Context Protocol (MCP) Toolkit, essential for managing AI/ML applications, including agentic AI and LLMs. By the end, you’ll be able to deploy AI models locally, create reproducible environments, and automate pipelines with Docker.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="fluxcdfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-ondevops"&gt;&lt;a id="fluxcdfortheabsolutebeginners_hands-ondevops" href="https://youtu.be/0pGfzwpCsWI"&gt;Flux CD for the Absolute Beginners - Hands-On DevOps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course introduces you to the world of GitOps and Flux CD, focusing on streamlining Kubernetes deployments through automation. You’ll begin by exploring GitOps concepts, followed by a comprehensive introduction to Flux CD and its core features. Hands-on demonstrations will guide you through the process of setting up Flux CD, understanding Flux CLI, and installing it on Kubernetes clusters.  Next, you’ll dive into deploying applications using Kustomize, Helm, and OCI Registry, learning the ins and outs of each tool to create efficient and scalable deployment pipelines. You’ll also explore Flux CD's advanced features such as image automation controllers, notification controllers, and its integration with monitoring tools like Prometheus and Grafana. By the end, you’ll gain valuable experience working with Flux CD’s UI and implementing security best practices to protect your deployment workflows.  Through practical demonstrations and real-world examples, this course equips you with the skills necessary to automate, monitor, and manage your Kubernetes deployments using GitOps and Flux CD. Whether you are an aspiring DevOps professional or looking to expand your Kubernetes knowledge, this course provides a solid foundation to take your skills to the next level.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="terraforminaction_buildandmanagecloudinfrastructure"&gt;&lt;a id="terraforminaction_buildandmanagecloudinfrastructure" href="https://youtu.be/PQjtQlKeKvg"&gt;Terraform in Action - Build &amp; Manage Cloud Infrastructure&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This comprehensive course takes you step-by-step through Terraform's core concepts, starting with the creation of basic Terraform templates. You'll learn how to use Terraform for managing a wide range of cloud resources, focusing on Azure services like Web Apps, SQL Databases, and more. With practical demos, you'll explore creating templates, deploying applications, and handling variables to tailor your deployments. As you advance, you'll delve deeper into Terraform's execution plans, state management, and workspace configurations. Learn how Terraform can automate deployments across different environments, streamlining your infrastructure management. The course also covers deploying container services, PaaS offerings, IaaS, and advanced services like Logic Apps and Azure Firewall with Terraform. By the end of the course, you will have the confidence and skills to manage cloud infrastructures efficiently using Terraform. Whether deploying single resources or complex multi-environment setups, you’ll walk away with valuable hands-on experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="dockerfordevelopers2026_microservicesprojectworkshop"&gt;&lt;a id="dockerfordevelopers2026_microservicesprojectworkshop" href="https://youtu.be/nsB7T4y9ELA"&gt;Docker for Developers 2026 - Microservices Project Workshop&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this comprehensive course, you will learn how to build and deploy a Dockerized microservices application, focusing on API development, authentication services, frontend integration, and deployment strategies. The course begins with an introduction to Docker and its essential tools, followed by detailed guidance on creating Dockerfiles, managing environment variables, and integrating databases and other services within your containers. You will explore key concepts such as Docker volumes, Nginx reverse proxies, Docker networking, and container orchestration. Step by step, you'll containerize various components of your microservices application, from the backend API to the frontend service, making them fully operational within the Docker environment. Throughout the course, you’ll receive practical challenges, including building a mailer service, to reinforce what you’ve learned. The course wraps up with a full deployment workflow, including pushing your code to Git, setting up a production server, and deploying your microservices application to a live environment. By the end, you’ll have the knowledge and hands-on experience to confidently develop and deploy production-ready microservices applications using Docker.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="hands-onciandcdwithgithubactions_absolutepractical"&gt;&lt;a id="hands-onciandcdwithgithubactions_absolutepractical" href="https://youtu.be/1D0kUBqlaXM"&gt;Hands-On CI/CD with GitHub Actions - Absolute Practical&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this course, you will gain practical experience in setting up and managing CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions. You will start by learning the fundamentals, including workflows, events, and triggers, before progressing to more advanced topics like self-hosted runners, Docker, Kubernetes, and custom GitHub Actions. The course is divided into sections that cover essential topics, including writing your first workflow, integrating popular tools like SonarCloud and CodeQL, and working with reusable workflows. Each section builds upon the previous one, taking you step-by-step through the process of automating development tasks. By the end of the course, you will be able to implement production-ready CI/CD pipelines that integrate security checks, deploy applications to Kubernetes, and automate testing and quality checks using a variety of tools and GitHub Actions features.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="introductiontodevopsfundamentalsforitandsoftwareprofessionals"&gt;&lt;a id="introductiontodevopsfundamentalsforitandsoftwareprofessionals" href="https://youtu.be/JVe-0NQv1t8"&gt;Introduction to DevOps Fundamentals for IT and Software Professionals&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course serves as a comprehensive introduction to DevOps, emphasizing its role in fostering collaboration between IT and software teams. Beginning with core concepts, learners will explore DevOps' evolution, its value, and its challenges. The course delves into the tools and practices that drive DevOps, including continuous integration, delivery, and deployment. You'll also discover the importance of infrastructure as code and how automation enhances team efficiency. In the second section, you will dive into key practices, including configuration management with Ansible and building situational awareness. Learn how to implement and monitor critical processes like continuous delivery, as well as managing environments with Docker and Kubernetes. The course concludes by preparing you for real-world industry applications, showcasing platforms like Jenkins, GitHub, and ServiceNow, and offering hands-on experience with automation tools like Terraform and Selenium. Throughout the course, you’ll gain insights into the tools that make DevOps a key driver for IT professionals today. Whether you're new to DevOps or looking to deepen your expertise, this course equips you with the foundational knowledge to succeed in DevOps-driven organizations and prepares you for a career path in this rapidly growing field.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="designandimplementciandcdpipelinesusingjenkins_hands-on"&gt;&lt;a id="designandimplementciandcdpipelinesusingjenkins_hands-on" href="https://youtu.be/NiI3_2Jq8m4"&gt;Design &amp; Implement CI/CD Pipelines using Jenkins - Hands-On&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course introduces the fundamentals of Continuous Integration and Continuous Delivery and explains how automated pipelines streamline development, testing, and deployment workflows. You will begin by exploring the core principles of CI/CD and understanding how automation improves collaboration and accelerates release cycles in modern development environments. The learning journey then shifts to Jenkins, one of the most widely used automation servers for implementing CI/CD pipelines. Through guided demonstrations, you will install Jenkins in different environments, explore its architecture, and navigate its interface. You will create Jenkins jobs, configure build triggers, automate testing processes, and integrate source code repositories such as Git and GitHub. You will also learn how plugins, agents, and nodes support scalable build automation. The course then moves into pipeline-based automation. You will design multi-stage pipelines and integrate tools such as Docker and Ansible to support automated deployments. Advanced topics such as credential management, conditional stages, and parallel execution will help you build efficient pipelines and implement practical DevOps automation workflows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="devopsandgenaiusingnetazureopenaiandgithub"&gt;&lt;a id="devopsandgenaiusingnetazureopenaiandgithub" href="https://youtu.be/x1_lNi82ucQ"&gt;DevOps and GenAI using .NET, Azure OpenAI and GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course begins by establishing a strong foundation in Generative AI within the DevOps ecosystem, explaining how AI enhances efficiency, decision-making, and automation across the software delivery lifecycle. Learners explore key concepts such as AI-assisted versus autonomous DevOps, along with critical risk considerations including hallucinations, model drift, and operational reliability. The course then transitions into practical implementation, where learners apply AI to real DevOps scenarios such as infrastructure as code, pipeline generation, testing strategies, release automation, and incident response. Through guided demonstrations, learners gain hands-on experience integrating AI into workflows using tools like .NET, Azure OpenAI, and GitHub, improving speed, consistency, and delivery outcomes. In the final phase, advanced topics such as enterprise governance, secure integration patterns, and agentic AI systems are explored in depth. Learners design intelligent pipelines, orchestrate AI-driven workflows, and implement autonomous agents with observability and control, enabling scalable, secure, and production-ready DevOps practices aligned with modern enterprise needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="opentelemetryinpractice_thecompleteobservabilitycourse"&gt;&lt;a id="opentelemetryinpractice_thecompleteobservabilitycourse" href="https://youtu.be/JnqbG2nv2Pw"&gt;OpenTelemetry in Practice: The Complete Observability Course&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course begins by establishing a strong foundation in observability, introducing metrics, logs, and traces along with service level objectives and error budgets. You will explore how modern systems are monitored and how different telemetry signals combine to provide deep insights into application behavior and performance. The journey then moves into building a complete observability stack using Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, and Grafana. Through guided labs, you will configure, deploy, and validate each component while integrating them into a unified system. You will also gain practical experience with OpenTelemetry fundamentals, including APIs, SDKs, collectors, and semantic conventions. As you progress, the focus shifts to real-world instrumentation of applications. You will implement metrics, traces, and logs using both automatic and manual techniques, understand context propagation, and apply advanced patterns. The course culminates in deploying everything to Kubernetes, verifying telemetry pipelines, and troubleshooting distributed systems in a production-like environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
