uch as Agile methodology and essential Jira terminology. The first section ensures you’re equipped with the foundational knowledge needed for the rest of the course. As you progress, you will delve into more practical elements of Jira. The course walks you through creating and navigating team-managed projects, offering hands-on practice in setting up Agile boards, customizing workflows, and managing issues. You will learn the differences between team-managed and company-managed projects, and how to configure and manage both types. The lessons emphasize real-world scenarios, helping you learn how to utilize Jira’s tools efficiently. In the final sections, you’ll gain an understanding of Jira’s administrative features. You’ll learn how to manage user roles and permissions, design custom workflows, and leverage automation tools to streamline project management. By the end of this course, you’ll have a solid understanding of how to configure Jira to meet your team’s unique needs, enabling you to manage projects with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="comprehensiveguidetoagilescrumfoundations"&gt;&lt;a id="comprehensiveguidetoagilescrumfoundations" href="https://youtu.be/5bqZ3W0DVOI"&gt;Comprehensive Guide to Agile Scrum Foundations: Explore Scrum: Methodology, Fundamentals, Concepts, Agile Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Scrum, a leading Agile framework, excels in project delivery through iterative, time-boxed approaches. This course is ideal for aspiring scrum masters or team members; it focuses on problem-solving and delivering value, making it a valuable choice to kickstart a successful career in Scrum.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Embark on a comprehensive journey into Scrum and Agile project management in our course. Starting with foundational principles, we move on to advanced concepts, guiding you through effective project management with Scrum. Furthermore, gain insights into orchestrating Scrum Teams, exploring the nuances of running projects with Scrum, and understanding key Scrum concepts. Moving on, you will immerse yourself in the dynamic flow of Scrum Events and equip your toolkit with essential platforms using our Scrum Toolkit series. Next up, explore popular tools such as Jira, Microsoft Teams, Microsoft Planner, and the newly introduced Trello. Stay ahead with the latest trends by incorporating ChatGPT into Scrum Teams for optimization and productivity, a cutting-edge dimension unveiled in our course. As you progress through the course, witness Scrum in practice, honing your skills through practical applications. With high-quality video lectures, downloadable handouts for quick reference, and engaging quizzes, this course provides a dynamic and interactive educational experience. By the end of the course, you will have a solid grasp of Scrum and Agile project management. You will be well-versed in the Scrum culture, proficient in managing projects using Scrum methodologies, and skilled in running projects with Scrum Teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilescrummasterlevel1_certificationprepandmockexams"&gt;&lt;a id="agilescrummasterlevel1_certificationprepandmockexams" href="https://youtu.be/WbcAgHWo8rQ"&gt;Agile Scrum Master Level 1 - Certification Prep and Mock Exams: Master Agile Scrum with Certification Prep, AI-Powered Insights, and Hands-On Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course equips you with the skills and knowledge to become a certified Agile Scrum Master. Learn through interactive demos, AI-powered insights, and practical exercises while preparing for the PSM I certification. Whether you're new to Scrum or enhancing your expertise, this course provides everything you need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course is designed to help you excel as an Agile Scrum Master, offering a blend of theoretical knowledge and practical application. You’ll begin with a foundational understanding of Scrum principles and frameworks, exploring roles, accountabilities, and events critical to successful Agile implementations. The course then delves into certification preparation with detailed insights into the PSM I exam and free resources to solidify your learning. Practical demonstrations form the core of your learning journey. From scheduling Scrum events and refining product backlogs to setting the Definition of Done (DoD), you’ll gain firsthand experience with essential Agile practices. Advanced sections introduce you to cutting-edge AI applications for process automation, team collaboration, and innovative product development. By incorporating software tools like Asana and leveraging interactive mock exams, this course ensures you’re thoroughly prepared for real-world challenges. With expert instruction and engaging resources, you’ll develop not just technical proficiency but also strategic insights to lead your team effectively. Whether using AI to streamline workflows or applying empiricism to drive innovation, this course equips you to thrive in dynamic Agile environments and advance your career confidently.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agileproductownerlevel1_certificationprepwithmockexams"&gt;&lt;a id="agileproductownerlevel1_certificationprepwithmockexams" href="https://youtu.be/Z1R04vgz_ng"&gt;Agile Product Owner Level 1 - Certification prep with Mock Exams: Gain Expertise in Product Ownership &amp; Scrum with Certification Prep, Mock Exams, and AI Tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unlock your potential in Agile and Scrum with a course designed for PSPO I® and PSM I® certifications. Explore principles, roles, events, and tools like Jira and Trello. Gain AI-driven insights, practical skills, and expert tips to excel in product ownership and project management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Embark on a transformative journey through Agile and Scrum methodologies with this expertly designed course. You'll start with an introduction to Agile principles, Scrum history, and the essential values that drive successful product ownership and team collaboration. Engaging videos and exercises ensure you grasp the fundamentals while providing insights into real-world applications. Delve deeper into Scrum roles, events, and artifacts, emphasizing their importance in creating efficient workflows and delivering maximum value. Explore how artificial intelligence revolutionizes product ownership by providing actionable insights, streamlining automation, and crafting innovative solutions. Hands-on demonstrations with Jira and Trello will elevate your skills in managing backlogs, planning sprints, and refining workflows effectively. Finally, put your knowledge to the test with certification prep for PSPO I® and PSM I®, featuring mock exams, practical tools, and expert tips to ensure you're exam-ready. The course equips you with the skills to lead Agile transformations and empowers you to implement Scrum practices seamlessly in your organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt12"&gt;Pay $12 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="completescrummastercertificationandagilescrumcourse"&gt;&lt;a id="completescrummastercertificationandagilescrumcourse" href="https://youtu.be/HZ0KhwhlIoY"&gt;The Complete Scrum Master Certification and Agile Scrum Course: Master Scrum and Agile Practices for Effective Project Management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn Scrum theory, roles, events, and artifacts through hands-on practice and expert coaching. This course prepares you for certification and equips you with Agile mastery to lead projects successfully.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Disclaimer: Scrum Open, Professional Scrum, Professional Scrum Master, Professional Scrum Product Owner, PSM, PSM I, PSM II, PSM 1, PSM 2, PSPO, and related terms are registered trademarks of Advanced Development Methods, Inc., doing business as Scrum.org. Our course and practice exams are neither endorsed by nor affiliated with Scrum.org. In this course, you will explore the Scrum framework and its evolution from traditional project management methods. Starting with the foundational theory, you’ll dive into key roles within Scrum teams—Scrum Master, Product Owner, and Developers—and their impact on project success. The course covers Scrum events and artifacts in depth, with practical examples and real-world applications. Through coaching videos and exam prep, you will solidify your understanding and gain insights for certification. The final module focuses on scaling Scrum for larger teams and projects, ensuring you can implement it effectively in diverse settings. Designed for aspiring Scrum Masters and Agile professionals, this course will equip you with the tools to lead teams, implement Scrum methodologies, and excel in Agile environments. Basic project management knowledge is recommended.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="masteragileestimation_toptechniquesforscrumandkanban"&gt;&lt;a id="masteragileestimation_toptechniquesforscrumandkanban" href="https://youtu.be/_Yl7TzI5pzQ"&gt;Master Agile Estimation - Top Techniques for Scrum and Kanban: Master estimation techniques to enhance planning and accuracy in Scrum and Kanban methodologies&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master Agile estimation with techniques like Planning Poker and Story Points. Learn to calculate team velocity and improve accuracy in Scrum and Kanban projects. This course will help you manage uncertainty and deliver projects more effectively. Whether you're new or experienced in Agile, you'll enhance your estimation skill.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In this comprehensive course, Master Agile Estimation - Top Techniques for Scrum and Kanban, you will dive deep into essential estimation methods used in Agile environments. Starting with the basics of estimation, you'll explore core techniques like Planning Poker, Story Points, T-shirt Sizing, Bucket System, and Three-point Method. The course provides a solid foundation in estimation best practices, with interactive exercises to help you apply these techniques effectively within your teams. You'll also gain insights into advanced topics, such as velocity-driven vs. commitment-driven planning, calculating team velocity, and using reference stories for enhanced accuracy. Troubleshooting common estimation challenges like multi-tasking, unstable teams, and ignoring uncertainties will also be covered. By the end of the course, you will be well-equipped to lead estimation sessions confidently, optimize team performance, and contribute to the success of Agile projects. This course is ideal for Scrum Masters, Agile Coaches, Product Owners, or anyone involved in Agile planning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="projectmanagementbestpracticesusingagileandscrum"&gt;&lt;a id="projectmanagementbestpracticesusingagileandscrum" href="https://youtu.be/2X6o0-dTLo4"&gt;Project Management Best Practices using Agile and Scrum: Master Project Success with Agile and Scrum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Unlock the potential of Agile and Scrum methodologies to transform IT project outcomes. This course dives deep into real-world cases of project failures, provides actionable insights into Agile adoption, and explores leadership strategies to drive team success. Empower yourself to lead change and achieve sustainable results.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course offers a transformative journey into the world of Agile and Scrum, tailored to project management professionals aiming to drive impactful results. Beginning with a look at common IT project failures, you'll uncover the root causes of missteps through compelling case studies. Alongside these lessons, you'll explore the core principles of Agile and Scrum, setting a strong foundation for implementing these frameworks effectively. As you progress, you'll tackle the challenges of Agile adoption, including resistance to change, inadequate communication, and traditional leadership hurdles. Detailed change management strategies and exercises help you evaluate your organization's readiness, establish buy-in, and foster a culture of empowerment. Real-world success stories highlight the transformative power of iterative development and teamwork, giving you a roadmap for achieving similar outcomes in your projects. The course wraps up with practical insights into modern leadership and team-building techniques. By understanding Agile’s servant leadership and applying the Shu-Ha-Ri learning framework, you’ll gain the tools needed to lead high-performing teams. With hands-on exercises like Planning Poker and Sprint Retrospectives, you'll refine your approach, ensuring every project you manage delivers measurable success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="completescrummastercertificationguide_masterscrumandachieveyouragi"&gt;&lt;a id="completescrummastercertificationguide_masterscrumandachieveyouragi" href="https://youtu.be/N5a9FjsO_Ak"&gt;The Complete Scrum Master Certification Guide: Master Scrum and Achieve Your Agile Certification - From Novice to Expert&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/368c2c0d36a40f3dc7526b320261ca500ca75666.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=578ea662184c5fcb2d2be1f9f40987b3"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This comprehensive course is designed for anyone looking to master Scrum. You'll learn Scrum fundamentals, Scrum events, artifacts, and the skills needed to lead Agile teams effectively. Master Scrum principles from scratch and get exam-ready with practical, scenario-based examples.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This Scrum training provides a comprehensive guide to mastering Scrum and Agile methodologies. You’ll begin by exploring the Agile Manifesto and understanding the differences between predictive and adaptive development approaches. The course introduces Scrum’s core values, roles, and responsibilities, including the Scrum Master, Product Owner, and Development Team. You’ll learn the significance of Scrum events like Sprint Planning, Daily Scrums, Sprint Reviews, and Retrospectives, and how to facilitate them effectively. Moving forward, the course covers Scrum artifacts such as Product Backlogs, Sprint Goals, and the Definition of Done, with real-world examples to strengthen your practical understanding. You’ll also explore key tools like Burn-Down and Burn-Up charts to measure progress. The course prepares you for the exam, providing strategies and guidance for addressing common challenges in Scrum. By the end of the course, you'll be equipped with essential Scrum Master skills like servant leadership, empathy, and active listening, preparing you to lead Agile teams confidently and effectively navigate Scrum challenges.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilereleasemanagementforscrumandkanbanteams"&gt;&lt;a id="agilereleasemanagementforscrumandkanbanteams" href="https://youtu.be/2itbG36BM6I"&gt;Agile Release Management for Scrum and Kanban Teams: Mastering Agile Release Strategies with Scrum &amp; Kanban&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discover how to drive efficient product releases in agile environments using Scrum and Kanban. This course walks you through vision-setting, roadmap design, planning strategies, and scaling frameworks. Perfect your release game with real-world exercises and expert guidance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In the fast-paced world of agile development, mastering release management is key to delivering value predictably and at scale. This course takes you through the complete agile release lifecycle for Scrum and Kanban teams. You’ll begin with core concepts such as defining your product vision, creating a product roadmap, and understanding your current release state. Through hands-on exercises, you’ll apply these concepts to your own product context, ensuring a personalized learning experience. As you move through the course, you’ll dive deeper into effective release planning, learning how to balance time, scope, and resources to meet deadlines. You'll explore the art of defining MVPs and MVFs, along with crafting both fixed-date and fixed-scope release plans. With a strong foundation in release strategies, you’ll then examine the essential infrastructure—continuous integration (CI), continuous delivery (CD), deployment pipelines, and testing strategies that ensure smooth releases. Finally, the course prepares you to scale agile releases across teams and organizations using frameworks like SAFe, LeSS, and Nexus. Whether managing single-team sprints or coordinating enterprise-wide releases, this course equips you with the tools and knowledge to lead successful agile releases at any scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrummastercertificationtraining_beamasterofscrum_becomeanexpertsc"&gt;&lt;a id="scrummastercertificationtraining_beamasterofscrum_becomeanexpertsc" href="https://youtu.be/R8OF1zLZp2k"&gt;Scrum Master Certification Training: Be a Master of Scrum: Become an Expert Scrum Master and Lead Agile Teams to Success&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/00f2a1eaa13c380e13afb1fb7aa21f092820f75e.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5efafb1cb96844d7a2de2db84a64cee3"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course provides a detailed, step-by-step guide to mastering Scrum, preparing you for the Scrum Master certification. You'll explore Scrum fundamentals, roles, ceremonies, and artifacts, with hands-on activities and real-world examples to help you become a successful Scrum Master.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course is your complete guide to becoming a certified Scrum Master and mastering Agile project management. You’ll start by learning the fundamental principles, roles, and values of Scrum, gaining a strong understanding of the framework’s core pillars: transparency, inspection, and adaptation. These concepts are crucial for applying Scrum successfully in any project environment. As you progress, you will dive deeper into Scrum events such as Sprint Planning, Daily Scrums, Sprint Reviews, and Retrospectives, learning how to facilitate them effectively. The course also covers Scrum artifacts like the Product Backlog and Sprint Backlog, teaching you how to manage them efficiently to ensure alignment with business objectives. Hands-on exercises will help reinforce your knowledge by applying Scrum in real-world situations. By the end of the course, you will have developed the skills needed to lead Scrum teams effectively, remove impediments, and foster a culture of continuous improvement. This training will prepare you for your Scrum Master certification and equip you with the tools to implement Agile principles and drive project success in any organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 id="bt18"&gt;Pay $18 or more to also unlock!&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrumadvanced_softwaredevelopmentandprogrammanagement"&gt;&lt;a id="scrumadvanced_softwaredevelopmentandprogrammanagement" href="https://youtu.be/EP2DzmpjZfw"&gt;Scrum Advanced - Software Development and Program Management: Take Your Scrum Skills to the Next Level with Advanced Techniques and Mastery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/5904aa83e020e6909b303e2dfe374e3273194704.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1b1830e1c69249b7a546653a0a6f3e32"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This advanced Scrum training is designed for professionals eager to master Scrum and elevate their skills to the next level. Learn the exact steps to become a certified Scrum Master and how to scale Scrum across multiple projects. Packed with actionable insights, this course helps you lead teams effectively and implement Scrum with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Disclaimer Scrum Open, Professional Scrum, Professional Scrum Master, Professional Scrum Product Owner, PSM, PSM I, PSM II, PSM 1, PSM 2, PSPO, and related terms are registered trademarks of Advanced Development Methods, Inc., doing business as Scrum.org. Our course and practice exams are neither endorsed by nor affiliated with Scrum.org. This advanced Scrum training course dives deep into Scrum methodologies, starting with a recap of the basics and progressing to advanced techniques. You'll learn the step-by-step process to become a certified Scrum Master, gaining the knowledge and experience necessary to excel in the role. The course focuses on real-world applications, particularly scaling Scrum across multiple projects using the Scrum of Scrums framework. It equips you to manage complex Scrum environments, ensuring alignment and efficiency across teams. Additionally, the course covers leadership skills and practical techniques such as sprint planning, backlog grooming, and retrospectives. With 72 reasons why Scrum works, you'll gain the tools to explain and influence others while strengthening your mastery of Agile principles. This course is ideal for aspiring Scrum Masters or professionals looking to refine their skills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="pmiagilecertifiedpractitionerpmi-acp_exploringagileprojectmanageme"&gt;&lt;a id="pmiagilecertifiedpractitionerpmi-acp_exploringagileprojectmanageme" href="https://youtu.be/YdgjwbN_J88"&gt;PMI Agile Certified Practitioner (PMI-ACP): Exploring Agile Project Management Essentials with PMI-ACP and Beyond&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/c9f80caaf017ef22ad95644b112d052f7b7a0f05.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b07bea2c3a8128eeba17262840bed1de"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Explore Agile practices with our comprehensive PMI-ACP course, designed to equip you with key Agile methodologies and tools for effective project management.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; The course begins with an insightful overview of PMI Agile Certified Practitioner (PMI-ACP), starting from the application process to exploring the dynamics of PMI Island for exam preparation. It provides a thorough understanding of the PMBOK Guide and compares predictive and adaptive methodologies, tracing the history of Agile and its basic concepts. The course then dives into various Agile methodologies, including Scrum, Extreme Programming, and Kanban, offering a detailed study of each. The course focuses on applying Agile principles in real-world scenarios. It emphasizes value-driven delivery, understanding business value, risk management in Agile projects, and Agile contracting methods. Learners gain insights into stakeholder engagement, adaptive leadership, and building high-performance teams. The course also covers adaptive planning, detecting and resolving problems in Agile environments, and continuous improvement techniques. The course wraps up with a comprehensive review of the essentials for the PMI-ACP exam, ensuring learners are well-prepared to excel in their Agile project management careers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="expertleadershipandmanagementinagileprojectmanagement_buildingcore"&gt;&lt;a id="expertleadershipandmanagementinagileprojectmanagement_buildingcore" href="https://youtu.be/TEJqIA-aYjE"&gt;Expert Leadership and Management in Agile Project Management: Building Core Competencies: Master Agile: From Historical Foundations to Core Principles&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course offers a comprehensive introduction to Agile, covering its history, principles, and values. You'll explore the transition from Waterfall to Agile and understand the fundamental concepts and working models that make Agile a superior choice for software development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Discover the transformative power of Agile methodology in this extensive course designed for technical professionals. Beginning with an in-depth look at the history and evolution of Agile, you'll gain a solid understanding of its foundational principles and values. You'll trace the journey from traditional Waterfall methods to Agile, comprehending the reasons behind the shift and the benefits it brings to project management. As you progress, the course delves into the core concepts and working models of Agile, providing clarity on when and how to apply Agile practices effectively. You'll learn why Agile development consistently delivers better software outcomes and explore its potential future in the ever-evolving digital business landscape. Practical exercises, such as reflecting on Waterfall vs. Agile, ensure you can apply theoretical knowledge to real-world scenarios. Furthermore, the course examines Agile project management's adaptability, helping you recognize the situations where Agile can be most beneficial. By the end, you'll have a comprehensive understanding of Agile and its application, preparing you to implement Agile practices confidently in your projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agileproductownerlevel2_comprehensivecertificationguideandmockexam"&gt;&lt;a id="agileproductownerlevel2_comprehensivecertificationguideandmockexam" href="https://youtu.be/yxSr1oRYBqc"&gt;Agile Product Owner Level 2 - Comprehensive Certification Guide and Mock Exams: Master Agile Product Ownership and Ace the PSPO II(r) Certification&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course equips Agile professionals with advanced Product Owner strategies aligned with Scrum principles. Covering product vision, backlog management, forecasting, and stakeholder engagement, it provides an in-depth understanding to succeed in the PSPO II® certification exam. Boost your career with expert insights and practical resources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Unlock the next level in your Agile journey with this advanced Product Owner training. Starting with a recap of fundamental Scrum principles, the course dives deep into essential topics such as empiricism, product vision, and organizational design. You'll explore advanced concepts like budgeting, release planning, and key metrics like Time to Market (T2M) and Current Value (CV), ensuring you’re equipped with the tools to deliver maximum value to stakeholders. The curriculum is thoughtfully structured to guide you through the nuances of managing product backlogs, stakeholder relationships, and release planning. Interactive videos and real-world scenarios help clarify complex topics such as agile-compatible contracts and cross-functional team dynamics. Special sections on mock exams and certification tips provide a focused pathway to acing the PSPO II® exam. Whether you're fine-tuning your understanding of Scrum artifacts or learning to navigate challenging stakeholder scenarios, this course provides the expertise and confidence to succeed as a Product Owner. By the end of this course, you'll not only be prepared to pass the PSPO II® exam but also to drive innovation and value within your Agile teams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilescrummasterlevelii_certificationprepwithmockexams"&gt;&lt;a id="agilescrummasterlevelii_certificationprepwithmockexams" href="https://youtu.be/FVIW8hnX11M"&gt;Agile Scrum Master Level II - Certification Prep with Mock Exams: Master Agile Leadership with Advanced Scrum Practices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Advance your Scrum knowledge and skills with this Level II course tailored for aspiring leaders in Agile environments. Covering advanced topics such as empiricism, team dynamics, stakeholder engagement, and risk management, this course also includes mock exams to ensure you're exam-ready. Become a certified expert in Scrum and lead with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Dive into the core principles of Scrum, exploring empiricism, Scrum values, and the intricacies of self-management. You’ll learn how to navigate the dynamics of Scrum teams, handle challenging stakeholder interactions, and foster collaboration across scaled teams. Each module features practical scenarios, quizzes, and actionable strategies to solidify your understanding. The course doesn’t just focus on theory—it’s a hands-on learning experience. Delve into the nuances of Scrum events, artifacts, and the all-important Definition of Done, ensuring you have a holistic grasp of every Scrum facet. Discover how to mitigate risks, tackle technical debt, and build resilient teams. Practical tips for exam preparation and mock tests are woven throughout to help you succeed on your first attempt at the PSM II® certification. By the end of this course, you’ll be equipped with the skills to lead Agile transformations confidently. With insights into leadership, organizational culture, and facilitation, this course ensures you’re not just exam-ready but also prepared to elevate your professional impact as a Scrum Master.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrumrepairguide_getagileteamsbackontrack"&gt;&lt;a id="scrumrepairguide_getagileteamsbackontrack" href="https://youtu.be/H-vyQCv253E"&gt;The Scrum Repair Guide - Get Agile Teams Back on Track: Restore Agile Team Performance with Practical Scrum Repair Techniques&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Many Scrum teams stall due to rigid practices, vague goals, or poor collaboration. This course helps you assess your team's health, uncover root causes, and implement proven solutions. Reignite performance by realigning with true Scrum values and practical techniques.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Agile success isn’t about rigidly following best practices—it’s about evolving your Scrum team in a way that fits your organization’s goals, structure, and people. This course begins by guiding you through a self-assessment to uncover why your team may be struggling, from misaligned goals to over-management and low morale. It identifies the common traps that teams fall into and explains how to correct them without abandoning the core framework of Scrum. You’ll move through real-world problem-solving sessions, combining strategic insights with hands-on exercises. You'll revisit Scrum’s foundational values and learn how to operationalize them in retrospectives and decision-making. You’ll fix your Product Backlog, restructure roles like the Product Owner, and uncover the real cause behind team stagnation. Developers, managers, and product leads will benefit from actionable strategies to rebuild accountability, collaboration, and clarity across the entire Scrum cycle. By the end of the course, you won’t just have a better understanding of Scrum—you’ll have a customized toolkit to repair dysfunctions, align stakeholders, and empower your team to deliver high-value results sprint after sprint. Whether you’re rebooting a struggling team or proactively optimizing performance, this guide is your blueprint to long-term agility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="masteringagilescrum_frombasicstoadvancedwithjiraprojects"&gt;&lt;a id="masteringagilescrum_frombasicstoadvancedwithjiraprojects" href="https://youtu.be/3oDb79JGg8c"&gt;Mastering Agile Scrum - From Basics to Advanced with Jira Projects: Master Agile, Scrum, and Jira for Modern Project Management Success&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gain a complete understanding of Agile Scrum and how to apply it effectively in real-world projects. This course explores Scrum roles, events, artifacts, and workflows, enhanced with Jira-based implementation. Learn to plan, execute, and refine agile projects with confidence and precision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In today’s fast-paced digital world, mastering Agile and Scrum is vital for effective project management. This course introduces the Scrum framework, its core values, and principles, exploring how Agile overcomes common challenges like poor coordination and inefficient planning. You’ll learn about the roles of the Scrum Master, Product Owner, and Development Team, and gain hands-on experience with creating user stories, estimating workloads, and defining the “Definition of Done.” The course covers managing product and sprint backlogs, conducting sprints, and using tools like burndown charts to track progress. You’ll also gain experience with Jira, setting up boards, epics, and tracking sprint performance. By the end, you’ll understand how to scale Scrum across multiple teams, facilitate Scrum ceremonies, and compare frameworks like SAFe and DAD. This course will help you lead Agile transformations, refine backlogs iteratively, and improve delivery and innovation for better project outcomes. Perfect for team leaders, developers, and project managers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="ai-enhancedscrummaster_automateanalyseandaccelerateagileworkflow"&gt;&lt;a id="ai-enhancedscrummaster_automateanalyseandaccelerateagileworkflow" href="https://youtu.be/HuJ-da2F8gQ"&gt;The AI-Enhanced Scrum Master - Automate, Analyse, and Accelerate Agile Workflow: Unlock Agile Excellence with Generative AI: Streamline, Automate, and Scale Scrum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The AI-Enhanced Scrum Master course teaches you to leverage Generative AI tools to streamline Agile processes. From backlog creation to sprint planning and ceremonies, you'll learn to automate tasks, boost team productivity, and integrate AI with tools like Jira, ChatGPT, and Microsoft Copilot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course is designed for Scrum Masters and Agile practitioners eager to embrace the power of Generative AI to supercharge their workflows. This course covers everything from automating backlog creation, user story generation, and sprint planning to enhancing Scrum ceremonies like daily standups. You’ll start by learning the fundamentals of Generative AI, including tools like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini, and how to apply them in an Agile context. With practical examples, you’ll explore prompt engineering, AI-driven prioritization, and how to integrate AI tools within Jira and other popular platforms. Key highlights include automating user story creation, generating acceptance criteria, and using AI for sprint tracking with burndown charts and dashboards. You’ll also learn ethical considerations around AI adoption and how to drive AI acceptance within your teams. By the end of the course, you'll be equipped to leverage AI for improved decision-making, team collaboration, and overall Agile success.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrummastercrashcourse_advancedpreparationforthepsmiicertification"&gt;&lt;a id="scrummastercrashcourse_advancedpreparationforthepsmiicertification" href="https://youtu.be/7hsfHRIl2-c"&gt;Scrum Master Crash Course - Advanced Preparation for the PSM II Certification: Advance Your Scrum Mastery, Leadership Skills, and Agile Thinking for PSM-A Certification&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/39c1e734d5672c436f4e8f5df73199d800141f70.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=012f519c34bfea317b97b3c46d2307c1"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course strengthens advanced Scrum Master skills required for the PSM-A certification. It focuses on leadership, product management, and professional Scrum practices beyond the basics. Designed to help experienced practitioners apply Scrum effectively in complex environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Disclaimer: Scrum Open, Professional Scrum, Professional Scrum Master, Professional Scrum Product Owner, PSM, PSM I, PSM II, PSM 1, PSM 2, PSPO, and related terms are registered trademarks of Advanced Development Methods, Inc., doing business as Scrum.org. Our course and practice exams are neither endorsed by nor affiliated with Scrum.org. This course builds on core Scrum foundations and revisits Agile values, Scrum theory, roles, events, and artifacts, then expands into people development, servant leadership, and real-world Scrum Master challenges. Emphasis is placed on decision-making, accountability, and applying empiricism beyond theory. As the journey progresses, the focus shifts to managing products with agility and supporting value delivery at scale. Topics such as product vision, backlog management, forecasting, release planning, and continuous quality provide a strong understanding of how Scrum Masters collaborate with Product Owners and Development Teams. The final stages emphasize mastery through advanced tips, coaching techniques, and organizational agility. Learners explore how to influence culture, enable evidence-based management, and foster sustainable, high-performing teams. Ideal for experienced Scrum Masters preparing for PSM-A, with basic Scrum knowledge and hands-on experience strongly recommended.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="aiprojectmanagementskills_scrummasterplusaipluschatgptplusjira_enh"&gt;&lt;a id="aiprojectmanagementskills_scrummasterplusaipluschatgptplusjira_enh" href="https://youtu.be/mKM9aK4WL-o"&gt;AI Project Management skills - Scrum Master+AI+ChatGPT+Jira: Enhance Scrum Master Practices with AI, ChatGPT, and Jira&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/236f74a3eb80b9094a6391e2f2d51249cdd00fca.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=2252d0384227e1f851e1ac0ad3c5e597"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course teaches Scrum Masters how to integrate AI into Agile project management. Learn to use ChatGPT, Jira AI, and modern tools to support product goals, backlog creation, sprint planning, and team facilitation. Gain practical, ethical, and repeatable AI-driven workflows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This course focuses on applying AI to real Scrum Master responsibilities using ChatGPT, Jira, and complementary AI tools. You’ll begin by understanding the role of AI in Agile environments, including prompt engineering fundamentals and how to select the right AI tools for project management tasks. Next, you’ll learn how to facilitate product goal creation and refinement using ChatGPT. The course then moves into AI-assisted product backlog management, where you’ll generate backlogs, acceptance criteria, and estimates, and seamlessly integrate them into Jira. You’ll also explore how Jira AI and ChatGPT can support sprint planning, subtask creation, capacity planning, and team commitment. In the final sections, you’ll apply AI throughout the sprint lifecycle. You’ll learn how to combine human judgment with AI outputs, generate meeting transcriptions, track actions in Jira and Confluence, and identify recurring blockers using ChatGPT. By the end of the course, you’ll be equipped to responsibly use AI to enhance Scrum facilitation, improve efficiency, and support better team outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="certifiedagilepractitionerpmi-acprtraining_prepareforthepmi-acprex"&gt;&lt;a id="certifiedagilepractitionerpmi-acprtraining_prepareforthepmi-acprex" href="https://youtu.be/cBXm68egvjE"&gt;Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP(r)) Training: Prepare for the PMI-ACP(r) Exam with Comprehensive Agile Training and Real-World Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/a212ff2ab55fd83322c9983b13612dc6e396a212.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=1f0756247f70ec700deaba4d582c2bff"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This comprehensive course will guide you through the Agile principles and practices required to become a Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP®). Gain real-world experience with Agile frameworks like Scrum, Kanban, and Lean while preparing for the PMI-ACP® exam. Hands-on exercises and project examples help reinforce learning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; The Certified Agile Practitioner (PMI-ACP®) Training course is designed to prepare you for the PMI-ACP® certification exam and help you gain a deep understanding of Agile methodologies. Starting with an introduction to Agile principles, the course dives into core practices like Scrum, Lean, Kanban, and eXtreme Programming (XP), and covers essential topics like Agile mindset, leadership, and team collaboration. Through detailed modules, you'll explore key topics such as the 12 Agile principles, project planning and execution, risk management, and product delivery. The course also offers practical insights into Agile frameworks, leadership styles, and how to foster a collaborative team environment. You’ll walk through real-world examples and projects, matched with the ACP exam content outline, to ensure your readiness. The course culminates in preparing you for the PMI-ACP® exam, providing essential guidance on exam application and how to navigate audit situations. By the end, you’ll not only be well-prepared for the certification but also equipped to apply Agile methodologies in real-world projects and work environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="agilescrummastercertificationbootcamp_psmiandcsm_transformyourcare"&gt;&lt;a id="agilescrummastercertificationbootcamp_psmiandcsm_transformyourcare" href="https://youtu.be/0fABxCVUB3c"&gt;Agile Scrum Master Certification Bootcamp - PSM I and CSM: Transform Your Career with Scrum Master Certification - PSM I &amp; CSM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/6520aa26365f270a1ae92c763b8a26a37e179000.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=0396eb32128ce22fa8df44058a5179a6"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Become an expert in Agile Scrum with this comprehensive certification bootcamp. Prepare for PSM I and CSM exams while mastering Scrum practices and frameworks. Build the skills to lead successful teams in Agile environments.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; This bootcamp provides an in-depth exploration of Agile Scrum and prepares you for the PSM I and CSM certifications. The course covers everything from Agile fundamentals to Scrum frameworks, teaching you how to effectively manage projects and teams in a dynamic environment. Through detailed modules, you'll explore Scrum's values, principles, and the various roles within a Scrum team, providing you with a well-rounded understanding of how Scrum operates in practice. The course then takes you through Scrum events, artifacts, and commitments, ensuring you’re equipped with the knowledge to plan, execute, and review Scrum processes successfully. Real-world examples and practical exercises help reinforce the learning, ensuring you understand how to apply Scrum in diverse scenarios. With expert guidance, you'll master techniques for managing backlogs, coaching teams, and resolving challenges, all while preparing for the certification exams. The final part of the course focuses on helping you pass the PSM I and CSM exams, providing tips, sample questions, and exam strategies. With step-by-step guidance, you'll be ready to confidently pursue certification and embark on a successful Scrum Master career.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="aiproductmanagerskillsforagile_aiproductmanagement_masteraiproduct"&gt;&lt;a id="aiproductmanagerskillsforagile_aiproductmanagement_masteraiproduct" href="https://youtu.be/E6ISdwN8UFo"&gt;AI Product Manager Skills for Agile - AI Product Management: Master AI Product Management in an Agile Environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/f654a93c3e5aa255cde6f546c827f41e5e992c26.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=5ea56572c0f98edfd0d09c774450b579"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course teaches AI product management skills for Agile teams, covering prompt engineering, competitive analysis, backlog management with Jira, and sprint planning. Learn how to create product roadmaps, define product strategy, and manage AI product lifecycles effectively in an Agile environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In this course, learners will dive into the core skills necessary for AI product management within Agile methodologies. Starting with the fundamentals, you will explore the birth of AI, understand why product managers need prompt engineering, and get hands-on with tools like ChatGPT. The first section offers a foundational understanding of AI tools and their uses in product management. The next section focuses on market research techniques vital for successful product management, including capturing user data and conducting competitive analysis. You will gain essential insights into analyzing user comments and reviews, preparing deep competitive analysis, and understanding market dynamics, which are crucial for making informed decisions in AI product management. As you advance, you'll learn to create a compelling AI product vision, strategy, and roadmap. Discover how to align product development with Agile principles and create a structured product backlog. Through hands-on exercises in Jira, you’ll gain practical experience in managing AI product backlogs, setting sprint goals, and using transcriptions to enhance collaboration. By the end of this course, you’ll be well-equipped to handle AI product lifecycle management effectively.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3 id="scrumandleaninaction_modernagileprojectleadership_masteragileandle"&gt;&lt;a id="scrumandleaninaction_modernagileprojectleadership_masteragileandle" href="https://youtu.be/K4teitv7UrI"&gt;Scrum &amp; Lean in Action - Modern Agile Project Leadership: Master Agile and Lean Methodologies for Effective Project Management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;img src="https://hb.imgix.net/39c4e6e9f28360a66d40625e9f864b5cb8d6ad37.jpg?auto=compress,format&amp;fit=clip&amp;h=350&amp;w=600&amp;s=b66d898ae508e5eb5e33c7a4809ce086"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course covers Agile and Lean principles, focusing on project leadership in real-world scenarios. You'll learn how to manage Agile projects, understand customer personas, and apply Lean strategies for process improvement. Gain essential skills in project estimation, prioritization, and Agile ceremonies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; In this course, you’ll start with a strong foundation of Agile and Lean principles, examining the core differences between Agile and Waterfall methodologies. The course delves into customer-centric project management, introducing you to customer personas, user stories, and acceptance criteria to ensure you're meeting client needs from day one. You will also explore MoSCoW prioritization and minimum viable product (MVP) strategies to ensure your projects stay on track and deliver value. As you progress, you’ll dive into managing Agile projects with a focus on roles, reviews, metrics, and risk management. Learn the best practices for building Agile work breakdown structures (WBS) and identifying the right tasks and milestones for your team. The course also provides a deep understanding of Lean concepts like work-in-progress (WIP) limits, Kaizen, and Little’s Law, essential for streamlining workflows and improving productivity. By the end of the course, you'll be equipped with actionable insights on both Agile and Lean practices that will help you lead projects successfully. Whether you’re managing a team or collaborating with stakeholders, this course will transform your approach to modern project leadership, making you a proficient leader who can effectively handle Agile projects and processes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
